.TH FOREST-GREETER 1 "July 2026" "forest-greeter" "Forest desktop environment"
.SH NAME
forest-greeter \- Qt-based login greeter for greetd
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B forest-greeter
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B forest-greeter
is a fullscreen, Qt-based login greeter for the
.BR greetd (1)
display manager, styled with the Forest theme system's
.I greeter.css .
It is configured as the
.I default_session
command in
.I /etc/greetd/config.toml
(installed as
.IR /etc/forest/greetd.toml )
and is run inside the
.B cage
Wayland compositor on VT1.
.PP
.B forest-greeter
is not intended to be run directly outside of a greetd/cage session.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/forest/greetd.toml
.RS
greetd configuration pointing it at
.B forest-greeter
running inside cage.
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR forest (1),
.BR cage (1)
